[00:36.08]Conversation One
[00:38.65]W: Hey, Steve, have you settled on a topic for Professor Miller's presentation yet£¿
[00:44.49]I'm still struggling to pick one. 
[00:47.21]Nothing really stands out to me so far, and the deadline is approaching.
[00:51.78]M: I'm thinking of doing it on digital calendars, you know, weighing the pros and cons. 
[00:56.93]They're pretty common in daily life, and almost everyone uses one nowadays, either for work or personal stuff.
[01:04.39]W: I just use a paper planner most of the time. 
[01:07.52]It's simple, never crashes, and doesn't require any set-up. 
[01:12.50]What makes you interested in digital calendars£¿
[01:15.84]M: Well, convenience is a big plus. 
[01:18.53]You can access them from any device with the Internet, like your phone or laptop. 
[01:23.73]Also, collaboration is easy¡ªsharing schedules with teammates for group projects or family events like reunions.
[01:31.86]W: That does sound helpful for coordinating deadlines and meetings. 
[01:36.24]But aren't there some drawbacks£¿ 
[01:38.30]Nothing's perfect, after all.
[01:40.29]M: Definitely. For one, they depend entirely on the Internet connection. 
[01:45.29]If you're in a remote area with no Wi-Fi, you cannot check or update your schedule at all. 
[01:51.67]That could be really frustrating when you're traveling.
[01:54.95]W: True. And I've also heard about privacy risks. 
[01:58.84]Storing everything online might lead to hacking or data loss.
[02:03.75]M: Exactly. Plus, technical issues happen¡ªtechnical errors or server downtime could make you miss an important event. 
[02:12.69]That would be a mess, especially for something like a job interview or exam.
[02:17.76]W: So accessibility and collaboration are the main pros, while dependence on the Internet, security concerns, and technical issues are the cons£¿
[02:27.50]M: Pretty much. 
[02:28.87]And I might add over-reliance on technology¡ªit can make us over-scheduled and less flexible for unexpected changes or spontaneous activities with friends.
[02:39.53]W: That sounds balanced and practical. 
[02:42.03]Do you want to practice our presentations together next week£¿
[02:45.94]We could help each other improve and polish our delivery.
[02:50.27]M: Sure thing. Let's meet at the library Tuesday afternoon. 
[02:54.06]I'll bring my outline, and you can share your draft too.
