[04:33.53]I'm so disappointed. 
[04:35.45]M: Oh, I see. 
[04:36.97]Have you considered ticket resale services£¿ 
[04:40.04]Sometimes you can still find tickets through authorized resellers even when official ones are gone.
[04:45.94]W: Really£¿ 
[04:47.15]I thought reselling was risky. 
[04:49.37]But I'm desperate now. 
[04:51.02]What's actually good about it£¿
[04:53.29]M: Well, for starters, you can often find better seats than what was originally available. 
[04:59.04]Resellers usually know exactly which seats they have, so you can pick a great spot.
[05:04.33]W: That sounds promising. 
[05:06.35]But aren't there extra fees£¿ 
[05:08.22]I don't want to pay way more than the face value just for convenience.
[05:12.67]M: That's the main drawback. 
[05:14.61]Additional fees can apply, and sometimes the buyer has to cover them. 
[05:19.05]But some resellers charge low or no fees if you search carefully.
[05:23.99]W: What about the tickets themselves£¿ 
[05:26.34]How do I know they're not fake£¿
[05:28.72]M: Certified resellers provide legitimate tickets since they have deals with official sellers. 
