[08:26.75]Passage One
[08:29.61]AI is cutting across boundaries as it is revolutionizing every sector in the world, including education. 
[08:38.31]It offers personalized learning experiences along with an efficient administrative framework.
[08:45.35]The new-age education methods using AI are to adapt courses according to each student's specific needs. 
[08:53.66]Adaptive learning software analyses data on the learning styles, pace, and performance of students to create customized curricula. 
[09:03.19]Intelligent tutoring systems act as virtual guides, providing mentoring on a one-on-one basis.
[09:10.80]Some professionals use AI to diagnose knowledge gaps and provide useful feedback. 
[09:17.21]With increasing advancements in natural language processing, such tutoring systems are becoming more conversational, simulating a human-like interaction that's much closer to reality.
[09:30.67]Additionally, the assessment is being simplified by the use of AI to grade both objective and subjective work. 
[09:39.06]Besides grading, AI gives feedback on student work to reflect on errors and enhance understanding. 
[09:46.67]As early as 2024, educational institutions reported that AI grading tools enable teachers to save 20 to 40 percent of time, freeing them up to focus more on teaching. 
[10:00.64]AI predictive analytics tools detect students' risk of underachievement or dropping out. 
[10:07.25]These systems analyse attendance, grades, and pupil data and report possible warnings. 
[10:14.14]We all know that the role of AI in education is becoming increasingly clear, but it should be used ethically. 
[10:21.96]For example, developers are trying to work to prevent bias in AI so that students will not be treated differently because of their gender, race, or socioeconomic status.
