[24:02.56]Engage in important conversations, keep up with current events, and keep a close eye on your business. 
[24:10.36]The more you introduce your brain to useful things, the more creative ideas it will come up with. 
[24:17.18]While you try to fill your brain with information, try to develop a sense of wonder and ask questions about everything. 
[24:25.29]Every question you ask gives you a new way to look at the world and a deeper understanding of it.
[24:32.10]Besides mental activities, physical exercise can also help. 
[24:37.13]Exercise isn't just good for your body but also for your brain. 
[24:42.28]Neurons, which are the brain cells that send messages, grow when you do cardio and power training. 
[24:49.46]Growing new neurons make your brain more powerful and complicated, improving intelligence.
[24:55.62]Do you know that meditation can also make you smarter£¿
[24:59.58]According to research, regular meditation can enhance your memory, focus, and even your IQ.
[25:07.41] Besides, your group of friends has a big impact on how smart you become. 
[25:13.05]Embrace smart, inspiring people who challenge your thinking. 
[25:17.48]Intelligence is infectious, and talking to people with great minds can make you smarter.
[25:23.71]Daily reading and writing can make a big difference, too. 
[25:27.78]Reading doesn't just teach you things; it also changes the way your brain works. 
[25:33.66]Brain scans have shown that reading just one book makes the brain work better and connect better.
[25:40.30] Writing isn't just a way to share your thoughts but also to make sense of them. 
[25:45.61]You can solve problems and transform your thinking process by keeping a journal, which lets you express your ideas in detail. 
[25:54.58]Your intelligence is a skill that you can improve and expand through daily habits. 
[26:00.37]By adding these practices into your life, you will not only boost your IQ but also enhance your problem-solving, creativity, and general cognitive performance. 
